On Windows, Chromium's folders and registry key are ilo's own. chrome_elf starts Crashpad, and
chrome.exe looks for a running browser to hand its launch to, from the user data folder
install_static names, before the core adds the app's --user-data-dir. As Chromium's, that was
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Chromium\User Data, which any other Chromium on the machine shares: ilo's crash
reports went with theirs, and a launch while one ran opened in it instead. As app/branding/name's,
it's %LOCALAPPDATA%\ilo\User Data, the prod app's profile folder, so its reports are in its own
Crashpad folder and a launch goes to the ilo that's running.

--- a/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
+++ b/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
@@ -21,7 +21,10 @@
 
 // The brand-specific product name to be included as a component of the install
 // and user data directory paths.
-inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Chromium";
+// browser_core: app/branding/name's, so the folders and registry key chrome_elf
+// and chrome.exe use before the app gives its --user-data-dir are ilo's, not
+// every other Chromium's on the machine.
+inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"ilo";
 
 // The brand-specific safe browsing client name.
 inline constexpr char kSafeBrowsingName[] = "chromium";
